WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.401 --> 00:00:04.524
- As morbid as it sounds, nobody knows

00:00:04.524 --> 00:00:05.872
when they're gonna die.

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:06.879
I'm fucked.

00:00:06.879 --> 00:00:08.561
I find that a little terrifying,

00:00:08.561 --> 00:00:10.678
and I just wanna shove my
life full of experiences

00:00:10.678 --> 00:00:13.078
before it's too late.

00:00:13.078 --> 00:00:17.095
So I'm gonna get as much of
my bucket list done as I can

00:00:17.095 --> 00:00:18.494
in one week.

00:00:18.494 --> 00:00:20.795
Something new every day.

00:00:20.795 --> 00:00:23.378
(upbeat music)

00:00:29.962 --> 00:00:32.893
I only have one week, so no big traveling.

00:00:32.893 --> 00:00:35.605
Marriage and kids, not
gonna do that this week.

00:00:35.605 --> 00:00:38.089
Go to outer space is just not
super realistic right now,

00:00:38.089 --> 00:00:39.824
so that's gone.

00:00:39.824 --> 00:00:42.213
After taking everything
into account I'm left with

00:00:42.213 --> 00:00:46.291
six items: learn to skateboard,
write a children's novel,

00:00:46.291 --> 00:00:49.379
get a tattoo, tell my
parents how much I love them,

00:00:49.379 --> 00:00:52.046
skydive, and play with a monkey.

00:00:53.592 --> 00:00:55.759
All right, let's go do it!

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:59.740
(triumphant music)

00:01:00.724 --> 00:01:02.591
Today I'm learning to skateboard.

00:01:02.591 --> 00:01:05.747
I have my helmet and my
elbow pads and I got a board.

00:01:05.747 --> 00:01:07.605
As well as my friend Steven
who's gonna teach me.

00:01:07.605 --> 00:01:09.081
- I really hope Megan falls.

00:01:09.081 --> 00:01:12.009
- My main goal for today is to
skateboard from here at work

00:01:12.009 --> 00:01:15.086
to the Arclight which is
where I park sometimes.

00:01:15.086 --> 00:01:17.129
Bucket list number one, let's go.

00:01:17.129 --> 00:01:18.682
I can do this.

00:01:18.682 --> 00:01:20.876
(relaxed music)

00:01:20.876 --> 00:01:21.877
- Okay.

00:01:21.877 --> 00:01:22.923
That's something to start with.

00:01:22.923 --> 00:01:24.334
(screaming)

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:27.172
(indistinct sped up talking)

00:01:27.172 --> 00:01:29.755
(upbeat music)

00:01:35.612 --> 00:01:36.808
Yeah.

00:01:36.808 --> 00:01:38.143
I think we can move on.

00:01:38.143 --> 00:01:40.152
You wanna go out front, hit some curbs?

00:01:40.152 --> 00:01:41.868
- Could we say another
word other than hit?

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:43.734
Oh, why am I so nervous?

00:01:43.734 --> 00:01:44.877
- You're gonna be fine.

00:01:44.877 --> 00:01:45.887
- What's that thing?

00:01:45.887 --> 00:01:46.886
- A curb.

00:01:46.886 --> 00:01:47.892
- No, no, there's a thing in the road.

00:01:47.892 --> 00:01:50.217
This, it's a leaf, okay.

00:01:50.217 --> 00:01:51.634
- Any other excuses?
- Nope.

00:01:51.634 --> 00:01:52.551
Ready, set.

00:01:54.374 --> 00:01:55.374
Skater girl!

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:57.945
Am I fast?

00:01:57.945 --> 00:01:58.994
(squeals)

00:01:58.994 --> 00:02:00.502
Okay, that was easy.

00:02:00.502 --> 00:02:01.674
I did it guys, it's over.

00:02:01.674 --> 00:02:02.507
Bye!

00:02:03.418 --> 00:02:05.241
(doo wop music)

00:02:05.241 --> 00:02:07.360
I'm in the gutter, cuz I'm trash.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.606
(screaming)

00:02:09.606 --> 00:02:10.895
- That was good.
- I can't skate to

00:02:10.895 --> 00:02:13.878
the Arclight constantly going (wailing).

00:02:13.878 --> 00:02:15.794
(chuckles) People will be so concerned.

00:02:15.794 --> 00:02:17.060
We'll just do it like once or twice more,

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:18.692
I can't imagine why I'd
need more than that.

00:02:18.692 --> 00:02:20.369
(playful music)

00:02:20.369 --> 00:02:22.536
(screams)

00:02:25.756 --> 00:02:28.065
I'm feeling very discouraged.

00:02:28.065 --> 00:02:29.211
This is just way more challenging

00:02:29.211 --> 00:02:30.574
than I thought it would be.

00:02:30.574 --> 00:02:32.211
I can hardly stand on the freaking board.

00:02:32.211 --> 00:02:33.709
Okay let's go.

00:02:33.709 --> 00:02:35.087
I'm ready.

00:02:35.087 --> 00:02:36.842
Okay, the time has come.

00:02:36.842 --> 00:02:38.895
I'm gonna do it.

00:02:38.895 --> 00:02:41.511
It's all the way down there,
seemingly into the oblivion.

00:02:41.511 --> 00:02:43.844
But into the oblivion we go.

00:02:46.227 --> 00:02:48.394
(beeping)

00:02:49.837 --> 00:02:51.358
(hip hop music)

00:02:51.358 --> 00:02:52.363
♫ What's the time, what's the time

00:02:52.363 --> 00:02:53.761
♫ What's the time, what's the time

00:02:53.761 --> 00:02:55.201
♫ It's time to tantivy

00:02:55.201 --> 00:02:56.931
♫ Tantivy

00:02:56.931 --> 00:02:59.503
♫ Come on it's no time to hide

00:02:59.503 --> 00:03:01.305
♫ You got to tantivy

00:03:01.305 --> 00:03:02.957
♫ It's time to tantivy

00:03:02.957 --> 00:03:05.056
I think I'm about halfway there.

00:03:05.056 --> 00:03:09.223
♫ No time to hide, it's time to tantivy

00:03:10.551 --> 00:03:11.492
♫ Relax no more

00:03:11.492 --> 00:03:13.277
♫ It's time to roll

00:03:13.277 --> 00:03:15.944
(horns honking)

00:03:17.853 --> 00:03:19.979
♫ We got to rise on up

00:03:19.979 --> 00:03:23.562
♫ We got to take our place

00:03:27.356 --> 00:03:28.189
Thank you.

00:03:42.967 --> 00:03:45.800
(uplifting music)

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:53.514
I'm exhausted.

00:03:53.514 --> 00:03:54.348
I feel like some people
will watch this video

00:03:54.348 --> 00:03:56.835
and just be like, "Big deal."

00:03:56.835 --> 00:03:58.264
(chuckles)

00:03:58.264 --> 00:04:00.586
But I was scared, this is like
what I was most afraid to do

00:04:00.586 --> 00:04:02.130
and I did it.

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:03.474
Day one is done.

00:04:03.474 --> 00:04:06.974
Let's go write a children's book tomorrow.

00:04:11.456 --> 00:04:13.069
I've always wanted to
write a children's novel

00:04:13.069 --> 00:04:16.285
so I could give back to kids what I got

00:04:16.285 --> 00:04:17.818
out of these books.

00:04:17.818 --> 00:04:20.544
I guess I've never gone
through with this because

00:04:20.544 --> 00:04:23.770
I just didn't think I was creative enough.

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:26.139
If I die and I haven't
written a children's novel,

00:04:26.139 --> 00:04:30.189
that's one more thing that I
would regret not having done.

00:04:30.189 --> 00:04:32.814
I think I want it to
be about mental health.

00:04:32.814 --> 00:04:34.474
I feel like a lot of adults
still don't understand

00:04:34.474 --> 00:04:36.556
certain aspects of mental
health, so I figure,

00:04:36.556 --> 00:04:39.598
let's start 'em young,
taking about depression.

00:04:39.598 --> 00:04:41.409
I'm not kidding, this
book is about depression,

00:04:41.409 --> 00:04:42.988
but it's gonna be great.

00:04:42.988 --> 00:04:45.571
(lively music)

00:05:00.711 --> 00:05:02.792
Oh! (chuckles)

00:05:02.792 --> 00:05:04.162
I did it!

00:05:04.162 --> 00:05:08.458
I titled my book Rita Rabbit
and the Invisible Injury.

00:05:08.458 --> 00:05:10.763
I don't have a ton of
children that I can share

00:05:10.763 --> 00:05:14.087
my story with at this moment,
so I am going to round up

00:05:14.087 --> 00:05:17.035
some coworkers and have story time.

00:05:17.035 --> 00:05:20.834
Rita Rabbit, Foxy Felicia
and Trusty the Turtle

00:05:20.834 --> 00:05:23.296
are all best friends.

00:05:23.296 --> 00:05:25.614
They play every single day.

00:05:25.614 --> 00:05:28.520
Rita Rabbit notices she hasn't been happy.

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:30.119
Oh I forgot to tell you,
this is about depression.

00:05:30.119 --> 00:05:32.246
(crowd laughs)

00:05:32.246 --> 00:05:33.322
- [Man] What a twist.

00:05:33.322 --> 00:05:35.798
- Foxy Felicia and
Trusty the Turtle stop by

00:05:35.798 --> 00:05:38.987
Rita the Rabbit's house,
but she shoos them away.

00:05:38.987 --> 00:05:42.311
Foxy and Trusty get tired of
Rita Rabbit not joining them.

00:05:42.311 --> 00:05:44.437
One day, Rita the Rabbit finds a

00:05:44.437 --> 00:05:46.225
piece of paper on the ground.

00:05:46.225 --> 00:05:49.671
It's an invitation to a party
Foxy and Trusty are throwing,

00:05:49.671 --> 00:05:52.088
and Rita is not invited.

00:05:52.088 --> 00:05:55.130
Rita goes to see Dr. Dolphin with her mom.

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:56.870
She hasn't been eating or sleeping.

00:05:56.870 --> 00:05:58.950
The doctor explains that
Rita has depression,

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:01.906
an invisible injury that hurts the brain.

00:06:01.906 --> 00:06:04.371
Dr. Dolphin explains that
even though you can't see

00:06:04.371 --> 00:06:06.831
the broken parts on the outside,

00:06:06.831 --> 00:06:09.397
the hurt that depression
causes to your insides

00:06:09.397 --> 00:06:12.939
can be just as painful
and difficult to heal.

00:06:12.939 --> 00:06:15.212
Felicia and Trusty ask how they can help.

00:06:15.212 --> 00:06:17.375
Rita asks for patience and understanding

00:06:17.375 --> 00:06:20.405
and for the friends to know
that depression is an injury

00:06:20.405 --> 00:06:23.140
Rita might be working on for a long time.

00:06:23.140 --> 00:06:26.881
With a deeper understand,
their friendship flourishes.

00:06:26.881 --> 00:06:28.461
The end.

00:06:28.461 --> 00:06:29.798
(crowd applauds)

00:06:29.798 --> 00:06:30.881
- [Woman] Aw!

00:06:32.846 --> 00:06:34.171
- Okay.

00:06:34.171 --> 00:06:35.484
Day two is over.

00:06:35.484 --> 00:06:37.648
This is gonna be a real book shortly.

00:06:37.648 --> 00:06:39.148
Link below to buy.

00:06:40.441 --> 00:06:42.728
Tomorrow, I get a tattoo.

00:06:42.728 --> 00:06:44.962
I haven't thought a lot about the pain.

00:06:44.962 --> 00:06:46.875
(rock music)

00:06:46.875 --> 00:06:49.975
I'm so excited but I also feel very ill.

00:06:49.975 --> 00:06:52.599
I brought my boyfriend
and my best friend here

00:06:52.599 --> 00:06:54.665
for moral support.

00:06:54.665 --> 00:06:57.150
I guess the reason I've
never gotten a tattoo is

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:59.541
fear of regretting it later.

00:06:59.541 --> 00:07:01.041
It's fine, lasers.

00:07:02.352 --> 00:07:03.185
No.

00:07:03.185 --> 00:07:04.046
To the chair.

00:07:04.046 --> 00:07:06.155
- Yeah, what are you
gonna get tattooed today?

00:07:06.155 --> 00:07:07.660
- I'm actually getting
a piece of advice that

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:11.042
my friend Mallory gave
me, which is, lean in.

00:07:11.042 --> 00:07:12.736
- I remember her sitting
at my kitchen table.

00:07:12.736 --> 00:07:14.906
She was telling me, "I
don't know what to do.

00:07:14.906 --> 00:07:16.275
"I just want to take this big leap into

00:07:16.275 --> 00:07:17.866
"this new adventure," and I told her,

00:07:17.866 --> 00:07:19.828
you just gotta lean in.

00:07:19.828 --> 00:07:22.408
Lean into the fear and do it
even though it scares you,

00:07:22.408 --> 00:07:23.870
cuz it's gonna be worth it.

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:25.108
- Okay, let's do it.

00:07:25.108 --> 00:07:26.898
There's gonna be a lot of
talking, I talk when I'm nervous,

00:07:26.898 --> 00:07:29.398
I also ask a lot of questions.

00:07:30.757 --> 00:07:32.473
- You good?
- No, no, no.

00:07:32.473 --> 00:07:33.532
No, no, no.

00:07:33.532 --> 00:07:34.751
Wait, wait.

00:07:34.751 --> 00:07:36.949
- Good talk, okay.
- No, no, no, no!

00:07:36.949 --> 00:07:38.303
- Ready?
- Yeah.

00:07:38.303 --> 00:07:40.109
- All right, here we go.

00:07:40.109 --> 00:07:40.942
(needle buzzing)

00:07:40.942 --> 00:07:41.775
One dot.

00:07:43.082 --> 00:07:44.427
- Are you kidding?

00:07:44.427 --> 00:07:45.427
- That's it.
- You serious?

00:07:45.427 --> 00:07:46.437
- Yeah.

00:07:46.437 --> 00:07:47.459
- That couldn't have been it, do it again.

00:07:47.459 --> 00:07:48.929
(chuckles)

00:07:48.929 --> 00:07:49.859
(needle buzzing)
- [Awz] How's that?

00:07:49.859 --> 00:07:51.950
- (chuckles) Oh wow.

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:53.708
I'm gonna be addicted after
this, cuz it's not nearly

00:07:53.708 --> 00:07:56.291
as painful as I thought it was.

00:07:57.433 --> 00:07:59.244
I could so have a baby after this.

00:07:59.244 --> 00:08:00.631
Oh, that's the pain.

00:08:00.631 --> 00:08:02.253
Look, it's on my arm!

00:08:02.253 --> 00:08:03.254
Here it is.

00:08:03.254 --> 00:08:05.214
It's perfect, it's
exactly what I imagined.

00:08:05.214 --> 00:08:06.447
(hands slap)

00:08:06.447 --> 00:08:07.980
I'm halfway done with my bucket list.

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:10.360
Now I have a whole body
ready for more tattoos.

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:11.852
Let's do day four!

00:08:11.852 --> 00:08:13.867
(upbeat music)

00:08:13.867 --> 00:08:16.130
I'm at my parents' house right now.

00:08:16.130 --> 00:08:19.346
If they die before I have
the chance to sit them down

00:08:19.346 --> 00:08:22.804
and make sure that they understood
how much they mean to me

00:08:22.804 --> 00:08:25.776
and how much I love them,
I would be devastated.

00:08:25.776 --> 00:08:28.004
So today, we're gonna
make sure that I never

00:08:28.004 --> 00:08:29.842
have to regret that.

00:08:29.842 --> 00:08:32.535
I brought you here to our kitchen table.

00:08:32.535 --> 00:08:34.045
Relax.

00:08:34.045 --> 00:08:37.063
This part of my bucket
list was to tell you both

00:08:37.063 --> 00:08:38.419
how much I love you.

00:08:38.419 --> 00:08:40.500
I know that people have their
parents die and they're like,

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:42.054
I wish I could just
tell them one last time

00:08:42.054 --> 00:08:45.340
how much I love them, and I
never wanna have that regret,

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:48.257
so, I just wanted to tell you guys.

00:08:49.483 --> 00:08:51.470
- This is my death thank you?

00:08:51.470 --> 00:08:54.303
- (chuckles) Yes.

00:08:55.174 --> 00:08:56.950
I didn't write a speech, I
don't have anything planned,

00:08:56.950 --> 00:08:57.955
that was kind of it.

00:08:57.955 --> 00:08:59.272
(chuckles)

00:08:59.272 --> 00:09:00.901
Don't die.

00:09:00.901 --> 00:09:02.585
- I don't plan on it anytime soon.

00:09:02.585 --> 00:09:06.846
- But we will hold onto
this forever and ever.

00:09:06.846 --> 00:09:07.929
- I love you.

00:09:09.446 --> 00:09:11.196
- Let's go eat lunch.

00:09:14.410 --> 00:09:16.124
(rock music)

00:09:16.124 --> 00:09:18.086
Today I'm skydiving.

00:09:18.086 --> 00:09:19.490
Diving from the sky.

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:21.739
Up there, onto planet Earth.

00:09:21.739 --> 00:09:23.654
I brought my mom, come here mom.

00:09:23.654 --> 00:09:25.013
Why did you insist on coming?

00:09:25.013 --> 00:09:26.661
- Because of the chances you take

00:09:26.661 --> 00:09:29.244
and that you follow your heart.

00:09:30.283 --> 00:09:31.292
- Okay, go away.

00:09:31.292 --> 00:09:32.919
This isn't the time for emotional shit.

00:09:32.919 --> 00:09:34.556
This is the time to jump from the sky.

00:09:34.556 --> 00:09:36.122
Let's do it!

00:09:36.122 --> 00:09:37.205
Freeze frame.

00:09:38.673 --> 00:09:42.590
(suspenseful orchestral music)

00:09:43.672 --> 00:09:45.334
Saying goodbye to my
mom, possibly forever.

00:09:45.334 --> 00:09:46.417
Just kidding.

00:09:52.695 --> 00:09:55.112
(rock music)

00:10:23.097 --> 00:10:24.014
- Go Megan!

00:10:25.781 --> 00:10:28.198
(rock music)

00:10:32.996 --> 00:10:35.163
(screams)

00:10:36.691 --> 00:10:37.524
- Bye.

00:10:38.732 --> 00:10:40.670
- [Megan's Mom] Meggy!

00:10:40.670 --> 00:10:42.645
- [Man] Welcome back down to Earth!

00:10:42.645 --> 00:10:43.645
- Holy shit.

00:10:43.645 --> 00:10:45.909
(groans) I wanna lie down.

00:10:45.909 --> 00:10:47.659
I don't feel my legs.

00:10:49.090 --> 00:10:51.223
Y'all, oh my god.

00:10:51.223 --> 00:10:54.125
You leave the plane and
you're just fucking falling,

00:10:54.125 --> 00:10:56.323
like I've never experienced
anything like that

00:10:56.323 --> 00:10:58.250
where you really are just like falling.

00:10:58.250 --> 00:11:00.004
The camera guy kept
grabbing my hand, like,

00:11:00.004 --> 00:11:01.706
"Yeah, smile," I was
like, "I can't smile!"

00:11:01.706 --> 00:11:04.008
I am still processing it.

00:11:04.008 --> 00:11:06.425
(rock music)

00:11:07.538 --> 00:11:09.477
Tomorrow's the day that
we play with monkeys.

00:11:09.477 --> 00:11:10.928
(grunts excitedly)

00:11:10.928 --> 00:11:12.677
We're gonna wash 'em,
we're gonna diaper 'em,

00:11:12.677 --> 00:11:14.073
it's gonna be so fun.

00:11:14.073 --> 00:11:16.738
(playful music)

00:11:16.738 --> 00:11:17.716
It's day six.

00:11:17.716 --> 00:11:19.981
It's the last day of the bucket
list, I can't believe it.

00:11:19.981 --> 00:11:21.954
This is something that
was on the top of my

00:11:21.954 --> 00:11:24.506
first bucket list, and I
can't believe that I get to

00:11:24.506 --> 00:11:26.282
make that dream come true today.

00:11:26.282 --> 00:11:27.724
Oh my god, it's a monkey.

00:11:27.724 --> 00:11:30.952
And I was told they're very
attracted to color and sparkle,

00:11:30.952 --> 00:11:32.763
which is why I put all of this on.

00:11:32.763 --> 00:11:34.342
This is gonna be a great day.

00:11:34.342 --> 00:11:38.001
Let's get down to some monkey business.

00:11:38.001 --> 00:11:40.576
Oh my god, I'm gonna cry.

00:11:40.576 --> 00:11:42.108
- This is Squirt.

00:11:42.108 --> 00:11:44.624
And Squirt here is gonna put
on her little bathing belt.

00:11:44.624 --> 00:11:47.541
You go ahead and jump in that bath.

00:11:49.272 --> 00:11:51.477
- Oh my god, it's a whole sink of monkeys.

00:11:51.477 --> 00:11:52.697
I don't know what to do.

00:11:52.697 --> 00:11:55.280
(upbeat music)

00:11:56.128 --> 00:11:57.211
Hi.

00:11:57.211 --> 00:11:58.632
- [Stacy] So what you wanna do, Megan,

00:11:58.632 --> 00:11:59.473
is tell her you love her.

00:11:59.473 --> 00:12:00.306
(smacks lips)

00:12:00.306 --> 00:12:01.319
Give her lip smacks.

00:12:01.319 --> 00:12:02.627
That's love.

00:12:02.627 --> 00:12:04.890
When people smile at a
monkey, that's aggression.

00:12:04.890 --> 00:12:07.008
- Oh no, I've been so aggressive.

00:12:07.008 --> 00:12:09.508
He is having a grand old time.

00:12:10.456 --> 00:12:12.134
- [Stacy] The one with the
funny hair do is Squirt.

00:12:12.134 --> 00:12:14.087
- Squirt!
- And she's 23 years old.

00:12:14.087 --> 00:12:17.261
- Wow, oh my god, we could be friends.

00:12:17.261 --> 00:12:18.739
(smacks lips)

00:12:18.739 --> 00:12:20.801
(mumbles in baby voice)

00:12:20.801 --> 00:12:22.359
- [Stacy] All right Megan, have a seat.

00:12:22.359 --> 00:12:23.749
Normally it takes awhile
for the monkeys to

00:12:23.749 --> 00:12:26.158
warm up to you but he's already excited

00:12:26.158 --> 00:12:28.015
about all your bling.

00:12:28.015 --> 00:12:30.682
(playful music)

00:12:33.080 --> 00:12:35.573
A little bit of monkey paw
tick's going on right now.

00:12:35.573 --> 00:12:38.119
Squirt is telling Marley
not to touch the food.

00:12:38.119 --> 00:12:40.286
(squeals)

00:12:41.480 --> 00:12:44.871
(playful music)

00:12:44.871 --> 00:12:46.416
- Oh, he's holding my hand.

00:12:46.416 --> 00:12:49.749
He's holding my hand like a little baby.

00:12:51.213 --> 00:12:52.640
Is this one keeping his
hand on me to say like,

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:54.649
you're my friend, don't pay
attention to anyone else?

00:12:54.649 --> 00:12:56.584
- [Stacy] Yes, Mo likes
you, he's claiming you.

00:12:56.584 --> 00:12:57.738
You're now his woman, Megan.

00:12:57.738 --> 00:12:58.736
- Sorry, Jake.

00:12:58.736 --> 00:12:59.741
- Hello my love.

00:12:59.741 --> 00:13:01.790
Eveyrbody, this is Chrissy the baboon.

00:13:01.790 --> 00:13:04.123
And Chrissy is 13 years old.

00:13:10.449 --> 00:13:12.788
♫ Best friends forever, me and Squirt

00:13:12.788 --> 00:13:16.147
♫ It's me and Squirt
forever starting right now

00:13:16.147 --> 00:13:18.784
- This has been the
absolute best way to cap off

00:13:18.784 --> 00:13:19.979
my bucket list.

00:13:19.979 --> 00:13:22.692
My five year old self
and my 25 year old self

00:13:22.692 --> 00:13:24.025
are so at peace.

00:13:25.598 --> 00:13:27.236
What a great week, guys.

00:13:27.236 --> 00:13:28.467
And those are all the words that I can

00:13:28.467 --> 00:13:29.915
conjure in this moment.

00:13:29.915 --> 00:13:33.332
(relaxed acoustic music)

00:13:37.069 --> 00:13:40.680
This past week has been
an absolute whirlwind.

00:13:40.680 --> 00:13:43.548
I accomplished things that
I only quietly dreamed about

00:13:43.548 --> 00:13:46.137
for my whole life, and
if I learned anything

00:13:46.137 --> 00:13:48.250
it's just that, there is no ready.

00:13:48.250 --> 00:13:50.198
There is no such thing as ready.

00:13:50.198 --> 00:13:53.010
There's only such a thing
as right here and right now.

00:13:53.010 --> 00:13:55.158
If you're too scared
to go pursue the things

00:13:55.158 --> 00:13:57.979
that you wanna do with your
life, what's the point?

00:13:57.979 --> 00:14:00.777
What is the point of living
if you're not gonna live it

00:14:00.777 --> 00:14:02.200
the way that you want?

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:04.347
I was ecstatic to cross off every item off

00:14:04.347 --> 00:14:06.765
that last bucket list, but there's still

00:14:06.765 --> 00:14:08.742
a million things that I wanna do.

00:14:08.742 --> 00:14:11.803
So, I made a new bucket list.

00:14:11.803 --> 00:14:14.553
(acoustic music)

00:14:21.419 --> 00:14:22.758
Hello again.

00:14:22.758 --> 00:14:24.299
What's up, man?

00:14:24.299 --> 00:14:27.049
(acoustic music)

